<title>USA: TCA Cable files $300 mln debt shelf offer.</title>
<headline>TCA Cable files $300 mln debt shelf offer.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>TCA Cable TV Inc, the nation's sixth-largest cable television operator, filed Thursday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission a shelf offering of up to $300 million in debt securities.</p>
<p>The Tyler, Texas company said proceeds from the sale will be used for general corporate purposes, including repaying outstanding debt.</p>
<p>No underwriters were named in the filing.</p>
</text>
